---
/**
 * Home.
 *
 * The portfolio is communicated through its two flagship findings, A4 and B1, and through
 * nothing else above the fold. Both are the same shape of result -- a number that looks
 * trustworthy and is not -- and stating them together is the argument the site is making.
 *
 * What deliberately does not appear here any more: test counts, continuous-integration
 * detail, canonical-environment detail and release history. None of it was deleted; it is
 * on the methods page, which is where a reader who wants it goes looking. Putting it on
 * the home page meant the first thing a reader met was an argument about evidence rather
 * than a finding.
 *
 * Every number below is read from a case artefact through the checked data path. Nothing
 * on this page is typed in by hand.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Figure from "../components/Figure.astro";
import KeyComparison from "../components/KeyComparison.astro";
import { checkedExhibit } from "../scripts/exhibits";
import { baseScenario, truth } from "../scripts/scenarios";
import { readJson } from "../scripts/public-data";
import { NAV, NOT_RUN, SITE_NAME } from "../scripts/site";
import { href } from "../lib/urls";
import * as fmt from "../scripts/format";

const f01 = await checkedExhibit("F01");
const base = await baseScenario();
const trueG = await truth();

interface B1Summary {
  b1_0_mathematical_baseline: {
    recovery: { permeability_thickness_recovered: number; permeability_thickness_true: number };
  };
  diagnostic_defect_visibility: {
    rows: Array<{ visible_without_truth?: boolean }>;
    silent_but_materially_wrong_count: number;
  };
}
const b1 = await readJson<B1Summary>("b1_summary.json");
const silent = b1.diagnostic_defect_visibility.silent_but_materially_wrong_count;
const seeded = b1.diagnostic_defect_visibility.rows.filter(
  (r) => r.visible_without_truth !== undefined,
).length;

const description =
  "Two synthetic studies of when a convincing reservoir-engineering answer is wrong: a near-perfect p/Z fit that overstates inventory, and a working well-test interpretation that stays convincing while its inputs are wrong.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={SITE_NAME}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/"
  nav={NAV}
  bareTitle={true}
  ogType="website"
>
  <h1>{SITE_NAME}</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Two questions run through this work: when does a reservoir-engineering answer look right
    and turn out to be wrong, and what would have had to be different for anyone to notice?
  </p>

  <p class="home__scope">
    Synthetic case studies, each reproducible from a committed protocol. Not field-validated.
  </p>

  <section class="finding" aria-labelledby="a4-h">
    <p class="eyebrow">Flagship finding — material balance</p>
    <h2 id="a4-h">
      <a href={href("/studies/a4/")}>A near-perfect straight line can still give the wrong inventory</a>
    </h2>

    <KeyComparison
      value={`${fmt.bscf(base.fittedBscf)} Bscf`}
      label="gas in place the p/Z fit reports"
      against={`${fmt.bscf(trueG.bscf)} Bscf`}
      againstLabel="known truth, withheld from the estimator"
      gap={`The fit that produced it has R-squared = ${fmt.rSquared(base.rSquared)}.`}
      tone="exception"
    />

    <p>
      The interpretation overstates the inventory by {fmt.percent(base.errorPct / 100)} and the
      fit gives no warning. <strong>Fit quality does not establish model adequacy.</strong>
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="finding" aria-labelledby="b1-h">
    <p class="eyebrow">Flagship finding — pressure transient</p>
    <h2 id="b1-h">
      <a href={href("/studies/b1/")}>A correct interpretation can still be wrong when its inputs are wrong</a>
    </h2>

    <KeyComparison
      value={fmt.outOf(silent, seeded)}
      label="seeded analyst errors that were materially wrong and moved no diagnostic"
      against={fmt.outOf(seeded - silent, seeded)}
      againstLabel="errors that either stayed within criteria or were caught"
      gap="The interpretation itself was established first: it recovers a withheld permeability-thickness and skin essentially exactly."
      tone="exception"
    />

    <p>
      A well-test inverse was shown to work on clean data, then attacked. Wrong rate, wrong net
      pay, wrong porosity, wrong viscosity: each passes straight through to the reported answer
      while R-squared stays at 1 to eight decimals.
      <strong>An interpretation can check itself against its own model; it cannot check the
      data it was handed.</strong>
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="home__evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-h">
    <h2 id="evidence-h">The A4 finding, in one figure</h2>

    <Figure
      id={f01.id}
      role="hero"
      number={f01.number}
      title="The fit that looks right, and the inventory it extrapolates to"
      svg={f01.svg}
      units={f01.units}
      interpretation={`Observed points and fitted line are visually indistinguishable over the observed interval, and the extrapolated x-intercept lands ${fmt.bscf(base.fittedBscf - trueG.bscf)} Bscf to the right of the truth.`}
      caveat={f01.caveat}
      longDescription={f01.longDescription}
      evidenceClass={f01.evidenceClass}
      svgDownload={f01.svgDownload}
    />
  </section>

  <section class="home__map" aria-labelledby="map-h">
    <h2 id="map-h">The studies</h2>

    <ol class="map">
      <li>
        <span class="map__stage">Stage A — inventory and material balance</span>
        <span class="map__body">
          <a href={href("/studies/a1/")}>A1</a> establishes the estimator,{" "}
          <a href={href("/studies/a3/")}>A3</a> measures what dominates its uncertainty, and{" "}
          <a href={href("/studies/a4/")}>A4</a> shows it failing while looking convincing.
          <a href={href("/studies/a2/")}>A2</a> cannot ship its exhibits: its inputs are
          someone else's data.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="map__stage">Stage B — transient interpretation</span>
        <span class="map__body">
          <a href={href("/studies/b1/")}>B1</a> establishes a pressure-transient instrument on
          a known answer, then measures which analyst errors it cannot see.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="map--future">
        <span class="map__stage">Not started</span>
        <span class="map__body">
          B2 through B6 — wellbore storage, build-up, boundaries, real-gas pseudopressure, and
          a case against data this project did not generate. Listed so the gap between what
          exists and what is intended is visible. None of it has been run.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="home__links">
      <a href={href("/methods/")}>How any of it can be checked</a> ·
      <a href={href("/about/")}>What this is, and what it is not</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="home__scope home__scope--foot">
    <strong>Synthetic throughout.</strong> {NOT_RUN.fieldData}
  </p>

  <style>
    .lede {
      max-width: 54ch;
      font-size: var(--text-lg);
      line-height: 1.4;
      color: var(--c-ink);
      margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
    }

    .home__scope {
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--c-ink-3);
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
    }

    .home__scope--foot {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-9);
      padding-block-start: var(--space-5);
      border-block-start: 1px solid var(--c-rule);
    }

    /* A finding is a section of prose, not a card: no border, no shadow, no rounded
       corner. Separation comes from space and from the eyebrow. */
    .finding {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-8);
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
    }

    .finding:first-of-type {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-7);
    }

    .finding h2 {
      margin-block: var(--space-2) 0;
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .finding h2 a {
      color: var(--c-ink);
      text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
      text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
    }

    .finding h2 a:hover,
    .finding h2 a:focus-visible {
      color: var(--c-blue-strong);
    }

    .finding p {
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
    }

    .home__evidence,
    .home__map {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-9);
    }

    .map {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-5);
      max-width: var(--prose-max);
    }

    .map__stage {
      display: block;
      font-size: var(--text-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--c-ink-3);
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-block-end: var(--space-1);
    }

    .map__body {
      display: block;
      color: var(--c-ink-2);
    }

    /* Future work is set back rather than boxed, so it cannot be mistaken for a result
       while still being legible. */
    .map--future .map__body {
      color: var(--c-ink-3);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
    }

    .home__links {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      color: var(--c-ink-3);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
